{"id": "EUVD-2026-105168", "enisaUuid": "2533df02-3299-3177-a90d-8d4136d166d2", "description": "json-smart through 2.6.0 contains an input validation bypass vulnerability that allows attackers to evade strict-mode trailing-data checks by inserting a literal 0x1A character. Attackers can append 0x1A and malformed content to pass JSONValue.parseStrict or isValidJsonStrict validation, creating parser differentials with downstream parsers like Jackson or Gson.", "datePublished": "2026-10-20T15:40:29", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-20T16:30:53", "baseScore": 6.9, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:N/VI:L/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/netplex/json-smart-v2/issues/302", "https://github.com/netplex/json-smart-v2/blob/v2.6.0/json-smart/src/main/java/net/minidev/json/parser/JSONParserBase.java", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/json-smart-through-2.6.0-strict-mode-validation-bypass-via-0x1a-character"], "aliases": ["GHSA-77mf-7xf5-w9wc", "CVE-2026-113602"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.45, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "ac5ba652-312a-3349-b069-32a10bdaa810", "product": {"name": "json-smart", "vendor": {"name": "json-smart"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22642.6.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "dc2e698e-4d18-39a5-85e9-e60172b27789", "vendor": {"name": "json-smart"}}], "isExploited": false}